# Local runs only: copy to .env next to agent.py, uncomment ONE group and fill in the key.
# The .env file is never packed and must never be committed.
# On the platform, add the model service under "Keys and network" (密钥与网络) instead.

# --- DeepSeek (OpenAI-compatible; address and model default to the values below) ---
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# --- any OpenAI-compatible service (Kimi Coding Plan, Moonshot, OpenAI, Zhipu, ...) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.kimi.com/coding/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=kimi-for-coding

# --- Anthropic ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Several groups filled in? They are tried in the order KIMI, OPENAI, DEEPSEEK, ... and the client moves on to the
# next one when a service stops answering. To use exactly one:
# AO_LLM_PREFIX=DEEPSEEK

# Run without the model stages (rules only):
# AO_NO_MODEL=1
